{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788122927,"nonce":"ps/5FCeoknwlYBkEMPyqzvwhEjk=","message":"ACCEPTANCE — verified personally on the BORGES bench, 2026-08-30. All four criteria met; `state:done`.\n\nShips: TimeDriver (the budgeted DoSingleTick advance engine), pause/unpause/advance verbs, deferred-result mechanism, Config, ThermalGovernor, journal-tap halt matchers, status.json advance/thermal blocks, selftest `letter_delay_ticks` (the deterministic mid-advance stimulus). Loop shape exactly per the 0.1 amendment: GameComponentUpdate slot, CurTimeSpeed pinned Paused, return every frame, \u003c=25ms budget, per-second quota, hard cap regardless of caller.\n\n**1. `advance ticks:60000` halts at exactly +60000 paused.**\n\n```\n{\"reason\":\"ticks\",\"tick\":60653,\"ticks_elapsed\":60000,\"wall_seconds\":60.73,\n \"avg_tps\":987.9,...} state:{paused:true}     (start tick 653: 653+60000=60653 exact)\n```\n\n**2. `advance until:letter` halts within one tick — measured ZERO ticks.**\n\nDeterministic stimulus: `journal-selftest {steps:[letter], letter_delay_ticks:3000}` queues a letter for tick+3000 (LetterStackTick drains the delay queue per tick — decompile-verified), then:\n\n```\nadvance {until:{letter:true}, timeout_ticks:100000} -\u003e\n{\"reason\":\"letter\",\"tick\":63653,\"ticks_elapsed\":3000,\n \"halted_on\":{\"def\":\"NeutralEvent\",\"label\":\"AutoRimmer selftest\",...},\"halted_seq\":23}\njournal seq 23: {\"tick\":63653,\"type\":\"letter\",...}   \u003c- same tick as the halt\n```\n\nArrival tick 63653 = 60653+3000 exactly; halt tick == letter tick. The matcher rides a synchronous tap on Journal.Emit, so the flag is set inside the very DoSingleTick that received the letter and the loop stops before ticking again — capture from LetterStack state per the amendment, never from letter-open.\n\n**3. Sustained holds \u003c= max_tps over 5+ min; an absurd request respects the hard cap.**\n\n`advance {ticks:400000, max_tps:99999}` -\u003e effective cap 1000 (`max_tps_effective:1000`):\n\n```\n{\"reason\":\"ticks\",\"ticks_elapsed\":400000,\"wall_seconds\":402.24,\"avg_tps\":994.4,\n \"slower_spans\":[[207950,209028],...,[216148,229361]], \"journal_seq\":[25,128]}\n```\n\n**994.4 avg tps over 6.7 minutes, never above the cap.** Mid-flight status.json showed `activeOp:\"advance:adv-long\"` + `advance:{ticks_done:19000,target:400000}` (the tick-delta liveness surface). The seven slower_spans are Cassandra doing her worst — colonist deaths, a Man in Black arrival, mad-animal fights, ~13K ticks of clamped danger around tick 216K — while the budget loop plowed through at full duty and REPORTED the storyteller's opinion instead of honoring or hiding it (the amendment's ruling, demonstrated on natural events). 103 journal events over the run; boot health stayed **0 errors / 9 warnings**. Shorter-window quota check: `{ticks:6000, max_tps:100}` -\u003e 58.7s, avg 102.1 — bucket-boundary measurement artifact on a 1-min window (quota is per-wall-second-bucket exact; the resolutions comment covers it), amortizing to \u003c0.5% over the 5-min window, where measured avg was 994 vs cap 1000.\n\n**4. Timeout path returns reason=timeout, paused.**\n\n```\nadvance {until:{letter:\"NoSuchDef\"}, timeout_ticks:5000} -\u003e\n{\"reason\":\"timeout\",\"tick\":74653,\"ticks_elapsed\":5000,...} state:{paused:true}   (+5000 exact)\n```\n\nExtras, same session: `pause` interrupted an in-flight advance (`reason:interrupted` + `was_advancing:true`, both at the same tick); a main-thread verb during an advance answered `busy` with progress detail; `unpause {speed:Fast}` took (`took:true`, status showed Fast/unpaused/ticking) and `pause` re-took. Every advance result returned `state.paused:true` — including timeout and interrupt paths.\n\nNot separately demonstrated, said plainly: `halt_on_error` (default on) shares the identical Notice/halt path the letter test proved, but no red error could be induced mid-advance (the selftest verb is busy-gated during an advance, correctly); and the thermal governor is inert on this machine (no sensor — see resolutions), so budget-halving ran only in code review, not live. Both wait for a bench with the sensors/need.\n\nFinal build note: the full battery ran on the build one commit before HEAD; the only diff is the empty-`journal_seq` rendering fix, and the final DLL re-verified the timeout and ticks paths end-to-end (`journal_seq:[]` on eventless advances).","files":null}]}